        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elizabeth Wordsworth, Christopher Wordsworth, John Wordsworth\n- Organizations: Anglican Church, St Hugh's College Oxford\n- Roles: Bishop of Lincoln, Bishop of Salisbury, liturgical scholar\n\nFacts:\n- Christopher Wordsworth was born on 30 October 1807 and died on 20 March 1885.\n- Christopher Wordsworth was an English bishop in the Anglican Church and a man of letters.\n- Elizabeth Wordsworth was the daughter of Christopher Wordsworth, Bishop of Lincoln.\n- Elizabeth Wordsworth was the sister of John Wordsworth, Bishop of Salisbury, and Christopher Wordsworth, a liturgical scholar.\n- St Hugh's College, Oxford, was founded in 1886 by Elizabeth Wordsworth as a women's college.\n- St Hugh's College, Oxford, accepted its first male students in 1986, its centenary year.",
